abjectness:
中：n. 悲惨（卑鄙；无耻）
英：n. The state of being abject; abasement; meanness;
   servility.

abominableness:
中：n. abominable的变形
英：n. The quality or state of being abominable;
   odiousness.

accordantly:
中：一致地, 相符地, 调和地
英：adv. In accordance or agreement; agreeably; conformably;
   -- followed by with or to.

acrimoniousness:
中：n. acrimonious的变形
英：n. The quality of being acrimonious; asperity;
   acrimony.

adaptedness:
中：适应性
英：n. The state or quality of being adapted; suitableness;
   special fitness.

adequateness:
中：n. adequate的变形
英：n. The quality of being adequate; suitableness;
   sufficiency; adequacy.

agreeingly:
中：adv. agree的变形
英：adv. In an agreeing manner (to); correspondingly;
   agreeably.

all-possessed:
中：a. 中了邪似的
英：a. Controlled by an evil spirit or by evil passions;
   wild.

allowableness:
中：n. allowable的变形
英：n. The quality of being allowable; permissibleness;
   lawfulness; exemption from prohibition or impropriety.

alterableness:
中：n. alterable的变形
英：n. The quality of being alterable; variableness;
   alterability.

andranatomy:
中：[医] 男体解剖学
英：n. The dissection of a human body, especially of a male;
   androtomy.

androgynism:
中：n. [动] 雌雄同体
英：n. Union of both sexes in one individual;
   hermaphroditism.

antiorgastic:
中：[医] 制欲的, 制欲剂
英：a. Tending to allay venereal excitement or desire;
   sedative.

antiputrescent:
中：a. 防腐的
英：a. Counteracting, or preserving from, putrefaction;
   antiseptic.

apocryphalness:
中：n. apocryphal的变形
英：n. The quality or state of being apocryphal;
   doubtfulness of credit or genuineness.

apparentness:
中：外观,显然,明白
英：n. Plainness to the eye or the mind; visibleness;
   obviousness.

apparitional:
中：a. 幽灵般的
英：a. Pertaining to an apparition or to apparitions;
   spectral.

approachableness:
中：n. approachable的变形
英：n. The quality or state of being approachable;
   accessibility.

araneous:
中：[医] 蜘蛛状的
英：a. Cobweblike; extremely thin and delicate, like a cobweb;
   as, the araneous membrane of the eye. See Arachnoid.

argumental:
中：a. 好争辩的, 辩论的（等于argumentative）
英：a. Of, pertaining to, or containing, argument;
   argumentative.

arthrodynic:
中：[医] 关节痛的
英：a. Pertaining to arthrodynia, or pain in the joints;
   rheumatic.

ascensional:
中：a. 上升的
英：a. Relating to ascension; connected with ascent;
   ascensive; tending upward; as, the ascensional power of a balloon.

avena:
中：燕麦属
英：n. A genus of grasses, including the common oat (Avena sativa);
   the oat grasses.
